Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• basin ‒ identify storms that occurred in the North Atlantic (`'NA'`).  
• season ‒ restrict the analysis to the 2020 season (`'2020'`).  
• sid ‒ unique storm identifier; used to group all track points belonging to the same storm.  
• iso_time ‒ timestamp for each fix; used to order points chronologically.  
• latitude / longitude ‒ geographic coordinates of each fix; converted to `GEOGRAPHY` with `ST_GEOGPOINT()` to compute distances.  
• usa_wind ‒ maximum sustained wind speed (knots) reported by the U.​S. agency at each fix; shown together with the cumulative distance.  

Main conditions that will be used  
```
WHERE basin = 'NA'
  AND season = '2020'
  AND latitude IS NOT NULL
  AND longitude IS NOT NULL
```  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑solution queries; run them in order (each limited to 20 rows where practical) to understand the data and finally obtain the requested answer.

