Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• basin ‒ identify storms that occurred in the North Atlantic (`'NA'`).  
• season ‒ restrict the analysis to the 2020 season (`'2020'`).  
• sid ‒ unique storm identifier; used to group all track points belonging to the same storm.  
• iso_time ‒ timestamp for each fix; used to order points chronologically.  
• latitude / longitude ‒ geographic coordinates of each fix; converted to `GEOGRAPHY` with `ST_GEOGPOINT()` to compute distances.  
• usa_wind ‒ maximum sustained wind speed (knots) reported by the U.​S. agency at each fix; shown together with the cumulative distance.  

Main conditions that will be used  
```
WHERE basin = 'NA'
  AND season = '2020'
  AND latitude IS NOT NULL
  AND longitude IS NOT NULL
```  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑solution queries; run them in order (each limited to 20 rows where practical) to understand the data and finally obtain the requested answer.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at 20 North‑Atlantic fixes in 2020
SELECT sid, name, iso_time, latitude, longitude, usa_wind
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct storms (sid) that formed in the North Atlantic during 2020
SELECT DISTINCT sid
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Storm names that appeared in the 2020 North‑Atlantic season
SELECT DISTINCT name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Number of fixes (track points) available for each 2020 North‑Atlantic storm
SELECT sid, COUNT(*) AS pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
GROUP BY sid
ORDER BY pts DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Add leg distance (metres) between consecutive fixes for one sample storm
WITH p AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time, latitude, longitude,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
  WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
    AND sid = (SELECT MIN(sid) FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
               WHERE basin='NA' AND season='2020')
)
SELECT sid, iso_time,
       ST_DISTANCE(geo, LAG(geo) OVER (ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
FROM p
ORDER BY iso_time
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Total travel distance (km) per 2020 North‑Atlantic storm
WITH p AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
  WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
        AND latitude IS NOT NULL AND longitude IS NOT NULL
),
legs AS (
  SELECT sid,
         ST_DISTANCE(geo,
                     LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
  FROM p
)
SELECT sid,
       ROUND(SUM(leg_m)/1000, 1) AS total_km
FROM legs
GROUP BY sid
ORDER BY total_km DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Top‑10 longest‑travel storms in the 2020 North‑Atlantic season
WITH p AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
  WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
        AND latitude IS NOT NULL AND longitude IS NOT NULL
),
legs AS (
  SELECT sid,
         ST_DISTANCE(geo,
                     LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
  FROM p
)
SELECT sid,
       ROUND(SUM(leg_m)/1000,1) AS total_km
FROM legs
GROUP BY sid
ORDER BY total_km DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Retrieve the SID of the storm with the 3rd‑longest travel distance
WITH p AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
  WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
        AND latitude IS NOT NULL AND longitude IS NOT NULL
),
legs AS (
  SELECT sid,
         ST_DISTANCE(geo,
                     LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
  FROM p
),
tot AS (
  SELECT sid, SUM(leg_m) AS tot_m
  FROM legs
  GROUP BY sid
)
SELECT sid
FROM tot
ORDER BY tot_m DESC
OFFSET 2                -- skip first two (1st and 2nd place)
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Build cumulative distance (km) for that 3rd‑longest storm (20 rows preview)
WITH storm_id AS (   -- get the SID first
  WITH p AS (
    SELECT sid, iso_time, ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
    WHERE basin='NA' AND season='2020'
          AND latitude IS NOT NULL AND longitude IS NOT NULL ),
  legs AS (
    SELECT sid,
           ST_DISTANCE(geo, LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
    FROM p ),
  tot AS (
    SELECT sid, SUM(leg_m) AS tot_m
    FROM legs GROUP BY sid )
  SELECT sid FROM tot ORDER BY tot_m DESC OFFSET 2 LIMIT 1
),
points AS (
  SELECT h.sid, h.iso_time, h.latitude, h.longitude, h.usa_wind,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(h.longitude, h.latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes` h
  JOIN storm_id USING (sid)
  WHERE h.latitude IS NOT NULL AND h.longitude IS NOT NULL
),
legs AS (
  SELECT *, ST_DISTANCE(geo,
          LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
  FROM points
)
SELECT sid, iso_time, latitude, longitude,
       ROUND(SUM(IFNULL(leg_m,0)) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)/1000,1) AS cumulative_km,
       usa_wind
FROM legs
ORDER BY iso_time
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL ANSWER – full track of the 3rd‑longest‑distance North‑Atlantic hurricane of 2020,
--                  showing coordinates, cumulative distance (km), and max sustained wind (knots)
WITH storm_points AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time, latitude, longitude, usa_wind,
         ST_GEOGPOINT(longitude, latitude) AS geo
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
  WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
        AND latitude IS NOT NULL AND longitude IS NOT NULL
),
leg_dist AS (
  SELECT sid, iso_time, latitude, longitude, usa_wind,
         ST_DISTANCE(geo, LAG(geo) OVER (PARTITION BY sid ORDER BY iso_time)) AS leg_m
  FROM storm_points
),
totals AS (
  SELECT sid, SUM(leg_m) AS total_m
  FROM leg_dist
  GROUP BY sid
),
third_longest AS (
  SELECT sid
  FROM totals
  ORDER BY total_m DESC
  OFFSET 2      -- 0‑based offset → 3rd place
  LIMIT 1
),
track AS (
  SELECT l.sid, l.iso_time, l.latitude, l.longitude, l.usa_wind,
         SUM(IFNULL(leg_m,0)) OVER (PARTITION BY l.sid ORDER BY l.iso_time) / 1000.0 AS cumulative_km
  FROM leg_dist l
  JOIN third_longest t USING (sid)
)
SELECT sid AS storm_id,
       iso_time,
       latitude,
       longitude,
       ROUND(cumulative_km,1) AS cumulative_distance_km,
       usa_wind AS max_sustained_wind_kt
FROM track
ORDER BY iso_time;
```

Executing the final query (Query 10) returns every fix for the hurricane that covered the third‑greatest overall distance in the North Atlantic during 2020, together with the cumulative kilometres traveled up to each fix and the corresponding maximum sustained wind speed recorded at those times.
